<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Cabinet — Windows VSTs on Linux</title>
<meta name="description" content="Wine packaged as a Flatpak, bridging Windows VST plugins into a Linux DAW, one prefix per plugin.">
<style>
:root {
  --bg: #fbfbfc;
  --panel: #ffffff;
  --ink: #16181d;
  --muted: #61656e;
  --line: #e3e5ea;
  --accent: #2f5bd8;
  --code-bg: #f2f3f6;
  --ok: #1a7f45;
  --gone: #a3341f;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root {
    --bg: #131519;
    --panel: #1a1d23;
    --ink: #e8eaee;
    --muted: #9aa0ab;
    --line: #2b2f38;
    --accent: #8aa9ff;
    --code-bg: #21252d;
    --ok: #62c78d;
    --gone: #ef8a72;
  }
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
body {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0 1.25rem 4rem;
  background: var(--bg);
  color: var(--ink);
  font: 16px/1.6 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
}
main { max-width: 47rem; margin: 0 auto; }
header { padding: 3.5rem 0 2rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
h1 { margin: 0; font-size: 2.1rem; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
h1 small {
  display: block; margin-top: 0.3rem;
  font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 400; color: var(--muted); letter-spacing: 0;
}
h2 { margin: 2.75rem 0 0.75rem; font-size: 1.15rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
p { margin: 0.75rem 0; }
a { color: var(--accent); }
.disclaimer { margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--muted); }
code { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
p code, td code { background: var(--code-bg); padding: 0.1em 0.35em; border-radius: 4px; }
pre {
  margin: 0.75rem 0; padding: 0.9rem 1rem; overflow-x: auto;
  background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px;
}
pre code { font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.55; }
.current {
  display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem 1.25rem; align-items: baseline;
  margin-top: 0.75rem; padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
  background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px;
}
.current b { font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 600; }
.current span { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }
.table-scroll { overflow-x: auto; margin: 1rem 0; }
table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; }
th, td { text-align: left; padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem 0.5rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; }
th { font-size: 0.78rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; }
td.commit code { word-break: break-all; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.78rem; }
tr.is-current td { font-weight: 600; }
footer {
  margin-top: 3.5rem; padding-top: 1.25rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted);
}
footer a { margin-right: 1rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>

<header>
  <h1>Cabinet<small>Windows VST plugins in per-plugin Wine prefixes — x86_64</small></h1>
  <p class="disclaimer">
    Packaging only. Wine and <a href="https://github.com/robbert-vdh/yabridge">yabridge</a> are
    other people's work; Cabinet bundles them and wires them to your DAW.
  </p>
</header>

<h2>Install</h2>
<pre><code>flatpak remote-add --if-not-exists cabinet \
  $flatpakrepo_url
flatpak install cabinet $app_id
flatpak run $app_id</code></pre>
<p>
  That last line opens the window. Every operation is also a command —
  <code>flatpak run $app_id --help</code> lists them.
</p>

<div class="current">
  <b>Cabinet $current_version</b>
  <span>published $current_date</span>
</div>

<h2>How it fits together</h2>
<p>
  Only Wine runs inside the sandbox. The halves your DAW loads — yabridge's chainloader
  and <code>libyabridge-*.so</code> — are never copied out of it: the DAW reads them from
  the installed Flatpak itself, which <code>enrol</code> grants it read-only. There is no
  setup step. A shim at <code>$$WINELOADER</code> is the whole boundary between the two.
</p>
<p>
  Each plugin gets its own Wine prefix under
  <code>~/.var/app/$app_id/data/prefixes</code> — its own C: drive, registry and
  dependencies. yabridge detects which prefix a plugin lives in on its own, so several
  run side by side.
</p>
<pre><code>flatpak run $app_id new serum
flatpak run $app_id install serum ~/Downloads/Serum.exe
flatpak run $app_id dxvk serum
flatpak run $app_id sync</code></pre>
<p>
  For a Flatpak DAW, run <code>enrol &lt;daw-flatpak-id&gt;</code> first and read what it
  prints: bridging into a sandboxed DAW needs permissions that are yours to grant, not
  Cabinet's to assume. <code>doctor</code> checks both sides afterwards.
</p>

<h2>Rolling back</h2>
<p>
  The last $history_depth releases stay listed. Pick a commit from the table and:
</p>
<pre><code>flatpak update --commit=&lt;COMMIT&gt; $app_id</code></pre>
<p>
  A plain <code>flatpak update</code> moves you forward again; <code>flatpak mask $app_id</code>
  makes the rollback stick until you unmask it. Everything is bundled in the commit, so any
  version still listed is still installable.
</p>

<div class="table-scroll">
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Cabinet</th><th>Published</th><th>Commit</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
$rows
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h2>Signing key</h2>
<p>
  Commits and the repo summary are signed. The remote pins this key when you add it, so a
  later unsigned publish is refused rather than installed.
</p>
<pre><code>$gpg_fingerprint</code></pre>

<footer>
  <a href="$homepage">Source and issues</a>
  <a href="$flatpakrepo_url">.flatpakrepo</a>
  <div style="margin-top:0.75rem">Generated $generated. GPL-3.0-or-later.</div>
</footer>

</main>
</body>
</html>
